From: HANPU5838 <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] module: tolerate CRC drift when enabling optional configs

The stock vendor modules were built against the stock config and record the
expected symbol CRCs in their __versions section. Enabling CFS_BANDWIDTH or
CGROUP_PIDS changes the CRCs of some exported symbols, which makes every
vendor module refuse to load and the device bootloops.

This patch keeps the vermagic check intact but accepts CRC mismatches, letting
the vendor modules load when the changed structures are not actually referenced
by them (cfs_rq/cfs_bandwidth/pids_cgroup are internal to the scheduler).
---
 kernel/module/version.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/module/version.c b/kernel/module/version.c
--- a/kernel/module/version.c
+++ b/kernel/module/version.c
@@ -52,7 +52,8 @@ int check_version(const struct load_info *info,
 bad_version:
 	pr_warn("%s: disagrees about version of symbol %s\n", info->name, symname);
-	return 0;
+	/* nx721j: tolerate CRC drift from CFS_BANDWIDTH/CGROUP_PIDS */
+	return 1;
 }
 
 int check_modstruct_version(const struct load_info *info,
